We begin by drawing a diagram.  Since $\triangle ABC$ is isosceles with $AB=BC$, altitude $\overline{BE}$ is also a median: $E$ is the midpoint of $\overline{AC}$.  Thus, $AE=EC=6/2=3$.

[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,E;
A=(0,0); B=(3,5); C=(6,0); D= foot(A,B,C); E=(A+C)/2;
draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D); draw(B--E); draw(D--E);
